# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore - sits at the repository root, which is also the build context root
#
# Effect: these entries never reach the Docker daemon as part of the build context.
# Size: node_modules holds ~15k files and .output is a build artifact, so excluding
# them leaves a context of a few tens of KB.
# Correctness: with "COPY . ." in the Dockerfile, an excluded file can never be
# copied into the image by accident.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The active mode is a denylist: everything is included except what is listed
# below. It is paired with the explicit COPY list in the Dockerfile, which is the
# safer combination: even if a line is missing here, the explicit COPY cannot pull
# the host's node_modules (with Windows-native binaries) into a Linux image. The
# cost is that a new top-level directory must be added either to the exclusions
# here or to the COPY list in the Dockerfile.
# =============================================================================

# Must never enter the image
node_modules
.output
.wxt
.env/.env

# Version control and temporary artifacts
.git
.gitignore
repomix-output.xml
stats.html
stats-*.json
web-ext.config.ts
*.log

# =============================================================================
# Alternative: an allowlist (ignore everything, then re-include what is needed).
#
# To switch, comment out everything above, enable the block below, and change the
# Dockerfile to use "COPY . ." - otherwise the allowlist achieves nothing, since an
# explicit COPY already copies only the files you name.
#
# Three hard rules; getting any of them wrong fails silently:
#   1. Use "*" and not "/" to ignore the context root. "/" marks the root directory
#      itself as excluded, after which no "!" exception is ever evaluated (the moby
#      patternmatcher does not descend into an excluded directory).
#   2. "!" cannot bring back a file whose parent directory is excluded. After "core",
#      a later "!core/foo.ts" has no effect - so only exclude top-level entries.
#   3. The last matching rule wins, so every "!" exception must come after the rule
#      that excludes it.
#
# With "COPY . ." the host's node_modules / .output / .env/.env are kept out only by
# the allowlist below: one missing line and host files end up in the image. That is
# its main risk.
#
# To check the context size, look at the "transferring context:" line of the build;
# with the denylist it should be a few tens of KB.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# # Ignore everything at the root first (use * and not /, see rule 1 above)
# *
# # Required for the build: dependency manifests and config
# !package.json
# !yarn.lock
# !.yarnrc.yml
# !wxt.config.ts
# !vitest.config.ts
# !tsconfig.json
# !.dockerignore
#
# # Sources needed for wxt prepare / tests / development
# !entrypoints
# !core
# !tests
# !public
# !docs
# !README.md
#
# # Note: nothing under .env/ needs to be re-included. The image does not copy
# # any project file, so no .env/ path is ever referenced by a COPY instruction.
# =============================================================================
